  & =1\\cdot 7+4\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =7-8+6 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b)=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c37b847b-0603-5e0f-8973-9dd05a27d3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c37b847b-0603-5e0f-8973-9dd05a27d3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436839} :answer-field/id #uuid "56dee8e9-07f4-5b22-acca-8f6df3bf286f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436849}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "661d9816-4244-5782-9d68-b93f1424eb3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-317348" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (b\\times a)$, if $b\\times c=⟨-2,5,4⟩$ and $a=⟨-1,3,2⟩.$\n\n$c\\cdot (b\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-1,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,5,4⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2+15+8 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (b\\times a)=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d1ac6eb-e3c3-5371-80e6-24c3f54f1da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d1ac6eb-e3c3-5371-80e6-24c3f54f1da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436831} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a5b05a0-2b4a-5a26-9708-cfdb631cd43b" :answer-field/key "field-1